# Estimate

An estimate of size or time, categorized by family, language, axis, and scope. One estimate is edited in place. Guess, sum, portion, and loc are subclasses.

◇

superclass_of_key: method

attributes:
    - key: scope
      name: Scope
      details: How the estimate is categorized.
      rules: enum of project, phase, cycle, proxy, added, modified, deleted
      type_spec: STRING
    - key: mean
      name: Mean
      details: The middle of the estimate bell curve.
      rules: "[unconstrained .. unconstrained] at 0.01 unit"
      type_spec: Real
    - key: variance
      name: Variance
      details: The shape of the estimate bell curve.
      rules: "[0 .. unconstrained] at 0.01 unit"
      type_spec: Real
    - key: low
      name: Low
      details: Lowest estimate based on the prediction interval.
      rules: "[unconstrained .. unconstrained] at 0.01 unit"
      type_spec: Real
    - key: high
      name: High
      details: Highest estimate based on the prediction interval.
      rules: "[unconstrained .. unconstrained] at 0.01 unit"
      type_spec: Real
    - key: prediction_interval
      name: Prediction Interval
      details: High/low range of interest, from 0 to 1.
      rules: "[0 .. 1] at 0.01 fraction"
      type_spec: Real
    - key: comment
      name: Comment
      details: Note about how the estimate was computed.
      rules: unconstrained
      type_spec: STRING
    - key: estimation_time
      name: Estimation Time
      details: When the estimate was made.
      rules: datetime
      type_spec: Nat

associations:
    - name: Uses Size Count
      details: Size metric this estimate is categorized by.
      from_multiplicity: any
      to_class_key: process/family/size_count_type
      to_multiplicity: "1"
    - name: Has Actual
      details: Recorded result that completes this estimate, added when the work is done.
      from_multiplicity: "1"
      to_class_key: actual
      to_multiplicity: "0..1"
